```sql
-- Two customers; only Ravi has placed an order.
CREATE TABLE customers (id INT PRIMARY KEY, name VARCHAR(40));
CREATE TABLE orders   (id INT PRIMARY KEY, customer_id INT, total INT);

INSERT INTO customers VALUES (1, 'Ravi'), (2, 'Neha');
INSERT INTO orders    VALUES (10, 1, 1200);
-- Neha (id 2) has no matching row in orders.
```

*Neha is the unmatched left-side row that exposes how each join behaves.*
